{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CegDHDmqnuPEi3DPZxw24","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"All three round-025 findings are closed and WI-579 is closed on driven evidence.\n\n**What I did**\n\n*Finding 1 (MAJOR) — the asserted full-suite green.* This one was correct, and it was the reason the close had to be reopened: a spec sitting in `docs/archive/work/complete/` asserts its Done-when list, and Done-when 5 (\"Full suite green\") had never been produced — every recorded unfiltered run carried one failure. I did not reword the criterion; I drove it.\n\n- Full unfiltered suite at `4332a073`, on a scratch worktree with `docs/stage` regenerated: **3349 passed, 25 skipped, 0 failed in 598.87 s**.\n- Re-driven at the closing tip `430a7fe8` (the close changed `docs/work/` and `docs/ratify/`, so the earlier run was a different tree): **3349 passed, 25 skipped, 0 failed in 625.13 s**.\n- The single node the branch tree still reds, `test_derive_stage.py::test_this_repo_s_committed_stage_is_current`, I drove **both ways** rather than argued: it fails on the committed tree and passes on the regenerated one at the same commit. It is **caused by this branch** (four Drafted rows move `drafted` 9→13 plus the fingerprint counting them) and benign because `docs/stage` is a declared `[generated]` artifact the trunk lane writes post-merge — every derived stage field is byte-identical across the two trees; only the bookkeeping census moves.\n\n*Finding 2 (MAJOR) — LLR-207.* Detail and Rationale now state standing system behavior; they scan clean for `WI-`, `OI-`, `D-<n>`, `round <n>` and date tokens. The history moved to the WI record and log fragment.\n\n*Finding 3 (MINOR) — IF-175.* `Data` went from 1034 chars to a 145-char typed seam signature (ceiling 160); the contract explanation was already in the row's `Notes`, so nothing was dropped to fit. `trace.py --strict-integrity` reports `interface-findings=0`.\n\n**Closed:** Deliverable filled before Context, `specref` clear, approval brief regenerated, spec moved to `docs/archive/work/complete/`, `check_trajectory: clean (532 done)`. Three commits, final one `59373fd5`, each carrying `WI: WI-579`.\n\n**Two things worth flagging:**\n\n1. My final commit touches `docs/log.d` only. I claimed that doesn't stale the review round — then verified it rather than asserting it, using the module this WI ships: `governing_identity` returns the identical 64-hex value at `430a7fe8` and `59373fd5`. So the round drawn against the closing tree still governs.\n\n2. A sharp edge I hit that cost a rejected commit: emptying a `## Deliverable` needs *two* newlines before `## Context`, because `parse_spec_deliverable` partitions on `\"\\n## Context\\n\"` and eats the single blank line. The parse failure drops the WI from the registry entirely, and the visible symptom is a cascade of unrelated-looking errors on *other* rows (`WI-545: predecessor 'WI-579' is not a work item`). I've recorded this and the `drafted`-moved verification recipe in memory, since the existing note's cheap benign test (\"per-phase and drafted match\") explicitly does not apply when a lane adds Drafted rows.\n\nI have not pushed — `push = \"human\"`."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":529,"cache_read_input_tokens":148224,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":529},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c6bb1ae3-4e06-4143-9db7-a341fa89ceea","uuid":"47034431-8c0d-47a8-970c-82bbc23be7f7","request_id":"req_011CegDHCZQxTsxuZjukyme6"}
